title: nemesis2_sanctum
---
Narrator:
The inner systems are quiet.

---

Narrator:
Not the quiet of abandonment. The quiet of deep infrastructure. Everything here runs at full efficiency, in silence, without waste.

There are no civilians visible. No traffic. Just purpose.

---

Narrator:
At the system's core, you find what the nemesis protects.

It is not a weapon. It is not a fortress.

It is a record. An archive of incalculable scope. Every campaign, every fleet, every commander who has ever crossed into this space.

---

Narrator:
Your entry is in it.

Every decision you have made since the first contact is in it.

---

Narrator:
Your security officer says: they've been compiling this for generations. We are one file among thousands.

She finds the files for your predecessors. Some of them end mid-sentence.

---

-> [Access the archive — take what you can]
    <<apply_effect "inner_sanctum_key">>
    <<chain_event "nemesis2_price">>
    Narrator:
    The archive is not encrypted against you.

    Narrator:
    It was designed to be read. They expected this moment.

    Narrator:
    Your security officer begins downloading. She is quiet for a long time.

    Narrator:
    Then she says: command is going to want to see this. And: some of this, they shouldn't see.

-> [Leave the archive intact — withdraw]
    <<apply_effect "nemesis_intel">>
    Narrator:
    You give the order. The fleet withdraws without taking anything.

    Narrator:
    Your security officer does not argue. She knows why.

    Narrator:
    Three hours later, a message arrives on a private channel. No identification.

    Narrator:
    It says: Thank you.

    Narrator:
    It says nothing else.

===
